        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "1. All Employees, whether individually or as a group, have the right to present their grievances to the appropriate management officials for prompt consideration. This procedure provides a means for the prompt and orderly consideration and resolution of Employee or Union grievances. In exercising this right, the Employees and the representative will be free from restraint, coercion, discrimination, or reprisal because they have filed a grievance.",
